                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Extract From Telegram, No. 153, of 5 February, From
                        Admiralty, London, to Admiralty, Paris</hi></head>
                <p>The Board considered that there are no suitable naval penalties that can be
                    applied to enforce compliance with armistice terms, and that any penalties
                    applied must be of a military character, and that they should represent this to
                    the Supreme War Council.</p>
            </div>
